Example: selecting only Assets:Fund changes when the investor contributes.
The journal and every command option except --accounts are identical to case 05.
Salary enters Assets:Cash on 2023-01-01, but that account is now excluded.
The FUND purchase on 2023-07-01 contributes 100 USD to the selected holding;
its closing value then is 100 USD and its value on 2024-01-01 is 120 USD.
Opening value is 0, net contributions are 100, and ending value is 120 USD.
Profit/loss is 120 - 0 - 100 = 20 USD and time-weighted return is 20%.
Both total return measures are 20% over the 184 days from purchase to end.
Annualizing either one gives (120 / 100)^(365 / 184) - 1 = 43.57%, versus
20% in case 05 when the selected cash received the salary at the start of
the full year. The earlier salary date is outside this selected portfolio.
"Instruments: 2" lists both explicit commodities, although the selected fund
account holds no USD.

========== CLI ==========

ledlight investment-performance --accounts Assets:Fund --include-commodities USD --include-commodities FUND --from 2023-01-01 --to 2024-01-01 --format text

========== FILE ==========

commodity USD
  default
  format 1,000.00 USD
commodity FUND
  format 1,000 FUND
account Assets:Cash
account Assets:Fund
account Income:Salary
P 2023-07-01 FUND 100 USD
P 2024-01-01 FUND 120 USD

2023-01-01 Salary
  Assets:Cash  100 USD
  Income:Salary  -100 USD

2023-07-01 Purchase
  Assets:Fund  1 FUND {100 USD}
  Assets:Cash  -100 USD

========== OUTPUT ==========

Investment performance from 2023-01-01 to 2024-01-01
Instruments: 2
Opening value: 0.00 USD
Net contributions: 100.00 USD
Ending value: 120.00 USD
Profit/loss: 20.00 USD
Time-weighted return (total): 20.00 %
Time-weighted return (annualized): 43.57 %
Money-weighted return (total): 20.00 %
Money-weighted return (annualized): 43.57 %

